And Whereas the public interest requires that Edward B. Russ, Chief of the Stenographic Section, Department of State, who, during the month of February, 1938, will reach the retirement age prescribed for automatic separation from the service, be exempted from the provisions of this section and continued in the service until March 1, 1939;

Now, Therefore, by virtue of and pursuant to the authority vested in me by the aforesaid section, I do hereby exempt Edward B. Russ from the provisions thereof and continue him in the service until March 1, 1939.

